{
  "statement": "The requirements GRN-01 to GRN-07 are essential for ensuring the sustainability of the ATM system. GRN-01 focuses on minimizing energy consumption during transaction processing, which is crucial for reducing the system's overall carbon footprint. GRN-02 mandates the provision of carbon footprint reports for each transaction, enhancing transparency and promoting environmentally conscious choices. GRN-03 emphasizes the use of energy-efficient hardware components, while GRN-04 ensures that transaction logging minimizes data storage requirements, thus conserving resources. GRN-05 offers clients an option for electronic records, reducing paper waste. GRN-06 promotes energy conservation by shutting down during inactivity, and GRN-07 emphasizes annual environmental assessments. Together, these requirements promote responsible resource use and align with modern sustainability goals.",
